WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:19.020
So let's now talk about the embrace of let
him die by the Republican Party.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.750
Lieutenant Governor Dan Patrick of Texas,
a Republican, of course.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:27.010
He's scaling up his war on commonsense and
his war on responsibility.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:32.240
He now says, hey, listen, with this Corona
virus thing and, you know, opening the country,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.570
there are more important things than living
to which I would say for who?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.660
Here he is on Tucker Carlson's program.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.200
Last night, I believe it was.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.290
But let's face reality of where we are.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.220
In Texas, we have twenty nine million people
we've lost.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.350
Four hundred and ninety five.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.640
And every life is valuable.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.250
But five hundred people out of twenty nine
million.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.850
And we're locked down and we're crushing the
average worker.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.190
We're crushing small business.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.500
We're crushing the markets.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.859
We're crushing this country.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:03.850
And what I said when I was with you that night,
there are more important things than living.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:08.700
And that's saving this country for my children,
my grandchildren, and saving this country

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.700
for all of us.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.700
And I don't want to die.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.700
Nobody wants to die.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.230
But, man, we've got we've got to take some
risk and get back in the game and get this

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.750
country back up and running.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.020
So was he refers to there.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.140
He did previously say he'd be willing to sacrifice
himself for the economy.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.320
And like I said before, that's fine if he
wants to sacrifice himself.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.410
But it's not up to him to sacrifice other
people for what he sees as saving the economy.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.200
Usually when they say save the economy.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.400
They really just mean the stock market.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.820
And it's similar here when Dan Patrick says
there are more important things than living.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:48.060
What he really means is there are more important
things to him than other people living.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.610
What is more important than living to individuals?

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.680
Now, there's another level of irony that I
would be remiss if I didn't mention today

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.290
about Dan Patrick.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.150
We can't ignore Dan Patrick's position on
abortion.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:04.641
If we are going to seriously analyze what
he is saying about Corona virus, Dan Patrick

00:02:04.641 --> 00:02:08.970
says, In the context of opening barbershops,
there are more important things than living.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.050
We've got to get the barbershop open.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.560
Living is less important.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.940
But when it comes to abortion, Dan Patrick
believes ending a pregnancy at eight weeks,

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.629
when you're talking about a clump of cells,
that's murder.

00:02:21.629 --> 00:02:24.599
He campaigned on ending abortion.

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:29.159
And then he flippantly says, you know, if
a few tens of thousands of grandparents have

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:34.980
to die, maybe even hundreds of thousands for
the stock market, there are more important

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.210
things than living.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:42.760
But if a clump of cells at eight weeks exists,
it must be protected as if it were the Secret

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.010
Service protecting the life of a president.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.270
The guy's a hypocrite.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.519
He doesn't appear to be a particularly good
person either.

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:56.359
And once again, with the religious right,
there is nothing more important than people

00:02:56.359 --> 00:03:01.780
until they are born, at which point it's OK
to go without health insurance.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.640
It's OK to go without food.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.749
It's OK to go without education, because we've
got to prop up the profits of all of these

00:03:07.749 --> 00:03:08.829
industries.

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:15.510
They don't care if you have to die to save
the Dow from dropping three extra points.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:21.659
But if you want to have an abortion, they
decide not the women and the people that would

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:26.110
be part of those individual decisions between
patients and doctors.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.799
This is what's so difficult about fighting
this.

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:31.109
They have the wrong moral code.

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:34.430
They're wrong on the facts and they don't
care.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:39.160
It's very difficult to fight against people
who share those characteristics.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:44.689
How do you fight someone whose entire frame
of reference and factual basis is not only

00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:48.230
incoherent, it's wrong and it indicates that
they are not empathetic people.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.540
It's a very, very difficult.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:55.370
The only real way to fight them is overwhelm
them with votes at the ballot box in November.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.180
As we've been speaking about yesterday and
today during the interview segment with Rachel

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:04.329
Bittar, Coffer convincing people to change
their mind is not an effective way to win

00:04:04.329 --> 00:04:05.329
elections.

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:06.620
It's particularly ineffective.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.390
When their moral code seems to be fundamentally
malfunctioning to them, it seems to work,

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.840
but to us it seems to be fundamentally malfunctioning.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.400
We've got to just find people and get them
to vote because these people are not going

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.400
to come around.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.550
Somebody who hears Dan Patrick say, listen,
barbershops are more important than grandma

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:26.950
living up.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.090
But don't you dare even think about getting
yourself an abortion.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.560
There's no arguing with those people.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.560
There just isn't.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:46.790
We've got to overwhelm them

00:04:46.790 --> 00:05:03.060
at the

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:52.830
ballot box.

